      "content": "that sounds like you're trying to have it both ways to stay neutral, but it feels like you're dodging the actual question. if a system is built on a logic that has been used to oppress people for centuries, isn't saying it has \"theoretical integrity\" just a way of legitimizing a fundamentally broken idea? if we're talking about absolute moral soundness in a modern context, isn't restorative justice just objectively the superior moral path?",
